James explored an engaging game mechanic for his character, Ekemon, seeking multiple belts of giant strength in an arcane library. He proposed two ideas: a series of keyword-based queries or a maze-like library with branching paths. I suggested a hybrid approach—a “living catalog” clue-web that fosters meaningful choices without confusion. It features 6–8 research locations, with each offering search approaches that yield clue tokens leading to the necessary details for identifying belt locations. I outlined a decision network, a clue card system for bearers and regions, and productive dead ends for when searches lead astray. Additionally, the mechanic incorporates a pressure track that introduces complications at high “Library Trouble” levels. To complement this idea, I provided a detailed prompt for creating a visually engaging map of the library for DALL·E.
